Tools for working with RIGHTCLICK MOAT001 GREEN.

Invoke one capability discovered for this object. Provider acceptance is not semantic success. Callers may supply structured provider-independent verification predicates; verified postconditions establish succeeded or failed semantic outcome. Without verification, accepted remains explicitly unverified. External, destructive, and unknown actions stay awaiting_user unless confirmed is true. This tool is part of plugin `RIGHTCLICK MOAT001 GREEN`.

exec tool declaration:
```ts
declare const tools: { mcp__codex_apps__rightclick_moat001_green_context_run(args: {
  // Capability id or exact title returned by context_actions.
  actionId: string;
  // Optional provider-independent structured capability arguments. Values are strings in the current schema slice.
  arguments?: { [key: string]: string; };
  // Set true only after the user confirms an action that returns CONFIRMATION_REQUIRED.
  confirmed?: boolean;
  // Legacy exact provider-returned-text postcondition. Prefer verification for generic semantic outcomes.
  expectedOutput?: string;
  // File path, http(s) URL, or plain text.
  item: string;
  // Optional caller-declared semantic postconditions. RIGHTCLICK evaluates them against observable state after invocation; provider acceptance alone is not success.
  verification?: {
  // Required provider-independent postconditions.
  predicates: Array<{
  // Optional byte threshold.
  bytes?: number;
  // Optional expected image height.
  height?: number;
  // Optional key, for example an extended-attribute name.
  key?: string;
  // Optional observation reference. Currently 'before' for before/after predicates.
  reference?: string;
  // Provider-independent observable predicate type.
  type: "text_equals" | "file_exists" | "file_readable" | "file_sha256_equals" | "file_sha256_differs" | "file_size_less_than" | "dimensions_equal" | "xattr_present" | "xattr_absent" | "metadata_value_present" | "metadata_value_absent";
  // Optional expected or forbidden exact value.
  value?: string;
  // Optional expected image width.
  width?: number;
}>;
  // Optional bounded wait for observable consequences. RIGHTCLICK caps this at 60000 ms.
  timeoutMilliseconds?: number;
};
}): Promise<CallToolResult>; };
```

